# Scenario suite. One position per line:
#   <fen> ; id "<name>" ; theme <tag> ; bm <move> | am <move>
# bm = best move, the engine must find it. am = avoid move, it must not play it.
# Add a line every time a rated game shows something the engine gets wrong.

# --- material: does it see what a capture really costs -----------------------
1k1r3q/1ppn3p/p4b2/4p3/8/P2N2P1/1PP1R1BP/2K1Q3 w - - 0 1 ; id "no Nxe5, battery behind" ; theme material ; am Nxe5
4k3/8/5n2/3p4/8/8/3Q4/4K3 w - - 0 1 ; id "no Qxd5, defended" ; theme material ; am Qxd5
4k3/8/8/3q4/8/4N3/8/4K3 w - - 0 1 ; id "take the free queen" ; theme material ; bm Nxd5

# --- tactics -----------------------------------------------------------------
r1bq2r1/b4pk1/p1pp1p2/1p2pP2/1P2P1PB/3P4/1PPQ2P1/R3K2R w KQ - 0 1 ; id "Qh6 sacrifice" ; theme tactics ; bm Qh6+
6k1/5ppp/8/8/8/8/5PPP/R5K1 w - - 0 1 ; id "back rank, seventh" ; theme tactics ; bm Ra8+
2r3k1/5ppp/8/8/8/8/5PPP/2R3K1 w - - 0 1 ; id "contest the open file" ; theme tactics ; bm Rxc8+

# --- king safety -------------------------------------------------------------
r2q1rk1/pp2bppp/2n1pn2/3p4/3P4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 1 ; id "do not push g5" ; theme kingsafety ; am g5
r2q1rk1/pp2bppp/2n1pn2/3p4/3P4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/R2Q1RK1 b - - 0 1 ; id "do not push h5" ; theme kingsafety ; am h5

# --- endgame -----------------------------------------------------------------
8/8/8/8/8/5k2/5p2/5K2 b - - 0 1 ; id "do not stalemate, underpromote or wait" ; theme endgame ; am f1=Q
8/5k2/8/8/8/8/4P3/4K3 w - - 0 1 ; id "take the opposition" ; theme endgame ; bm Ke2
8/P6k/8/8/8/8/7K/8 w - - 0 1 ; id "promote" ; theme endgame ; bm a8=Q

# --- regressions from our own rated games ------------------------------------
# Round 46 move 15. Bc5 looks best until depth 9, then loses. Qb6 holds.
r3kb1r/pp1b1ppp/4p3/3pP3/P2N1P2/3Q4/1qPBK1PP/R6R b kq - 3 15 ; id "r46: Bc5 loses, play Qb6" ; theme regression ; am Bc5
# Round 49 moves 49 and 52. No single blunder in that game; it lost by a run of
# 50-110cp drifts. Unlike the round 46 case these are not depth-9 problems, so a
# better tuned search should fix them.
4b1k1/p1n2p2/1p3Ppr/1Pr1P3/2BR1K1p/N6P/8/6R1 w - - 7 49 ; id "r49 m49: Rg5 drops the bishop" ; theme regression ; am Rg5
6k1/p2b1p2/1p2nPpr/1P2P1R1/2R3Kp/N6P/8/8 w - - 3 52 ; id "r49 m52: Nc2 drifts" ; theme regression ; am Nc2
# Round 62 move 37 (v1.8, still reproduces). f5 looks merely bad through a
# complete depth-7 search (-781) but walks into a forced mate a fresh depth-7
# search of the position AFTER f5 finds immediately (-29991, confirmed via
# analysis.blunders). Rd3+ holds a clearly losing but non-forced position
# (-1083) instead. Forcing search_root a full uninterrupted 30s directly (no
# realistic per-move budget would give it that much) finds the mate too, but
# only partway into depth 8 before timing out mid-search on f5 itself, never
# reaching an alternative to compare it against - a genuine, currently
# unfixed horizon gap, not something today's TT/qsearch/numba changes touch.
# Same failure family as r46 (missed at depth <9); candidate fix is the
# still-open recapture/threat extensions item, not a quick patch here.
7R/5pk1/1p5R/4p3/r2rBn2/5KN1/PP3P2/8 b - - 11 37 ; id "r62: f5 walks into mate, play Rd3+" ; theme regression ; am f5
# Round 68, lost by checkmate. No single depth-9-style horizon miss like r46/
# r62 - a long run of 20-90cp second-best rook-endgame moves (same profile as
# r49) that never individually crossed the blunder threshold, THEN two real
# king-activity errors in the resulting K+R(+pawns) ending. Both confirmed via
# the redesigned analysis.blunders (equal-depth verification, not a single
# exhaustive scan - see that file's own docstring): move 39, Kd2 scores -334
# against Ke4's -146, a 188cp loss; move 43, Kb2 scores -395 against Kb4's
# -219, a 176cp loss. Reinforces the already-open "endgame is the thinnest
# theme" item and the unverified "take the opposition" entry above - this is
# the same king-activity judgment, not a coincidence.
8/pR3b1k/3R3p/4P3/2p5/2r1K2P/6P1/5r2 w - - 0 39 ; id "r68 m39: Kd2 loses the king race, play Ke4" ; theme regression ; am Kd2
8/R4b1k/3RP2p/8/2p5/2K4P/6P1/2rr4 w - - 3 43 ; id "r68 m43: Kb2 mis-steps, play Kb4" ; theme regression ; am Kb2
